VALUES (579, '2', $t$ASK 579: the re-call reply blocks of nine Extract nodes are served from the Shared Library$t$,
  $t$Nine engine nodes each hold one large block that reads a debater's re-call reply: the `__O423` statement in C2B, D3B and C3B Extract, and the call inside `try{__X2=(()=>{...})()[0].json;}` in C4G, C3G, C1B, D2B, D4B and C4B Extract. The nine texts share most of their lines. Store each line once in the Shared Library and let each node rebuild its own text, byte for byte. Expected effect: 44,229 characters less stored while the child keeps its library copy, 114,298 once ASK 578 removes that copy (measured today, section 5); one place to edit a line the nine nodes share. No behaviour changes: no prompt text, no reasoning setting, no check and no output. (plan rev 2, section 1 OBJECTIVE, fairjudge/w3/a579/ASK579_plan_rev2.md md5 922b1a04)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 at 17:43 CST 2026-11-24 on the operator's press and read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 11775, 11781; audit 41763). Engine 20db58ee to 3afa1c1f: nine Extract nodes and the Shared Library changed; child 74353c40 to cd97165c: the Shared Library only; library a3c1e42f5b0ebda6, 3,852 lines, map ed7212a3189a4565. IN PART because the plan asks for the manual entry and two clean live runs, and neither exists, and one path is shown by no run. SHOWN: t579.js on the base, 99 checks, ALL PASS (W4, and W1's own rebuild, byte-equal targets); C6: each of the nine nodes, run offline on the stored inputs of run 42071, gives the same output as before, 9 of 9, on the live code, on the target and on the fetch-back; standing set 31 PASS, 0 FAIL; pair Library Check PASSES. NOT SHOWN: a re-call through one of the six try nodes (in run 42071 a re-call ran in C2B and C3B Extract only; Wall 11756). Measured: the nine nodes go from 226,060 to 41,693 characters and each library gains 70,069; the net saving was 44,229 with the child's copy and is 114,298 since ASK 578 removed that copy (19:08 CST, audit 41852). Stated cost (W1's plan note N1): the new entries reuse 37 existing library lines that 54 existing MAP entries serve too, so a later edit of one of those lines changes the nine nodes as well. The write card of 16:35 CST was answered "Wait for the 611 run"; the write followed run 42373 on a second card, and that run was later found NOT clean for ASK 611 (Wall 11779; W1's caution in Wall 11781). ASK 579 neither caused nor fixed that defect (W4, Wall 11778). Run 42373 ran on engine 20db58ee, before this write, and does not exercise it. RUN REVISION 42517 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed or that a path is unexercised, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42517-5yb0fmgv (debate_results fd0edbff, row saved 22:11 CST 2026-11-24; launch 21:50 CST; engine 2df7f6fa and child aad0ad9c by the write records; openai/gpt-6.2-sol as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; all eight rounds stored; THE PANEL FAILED at Panel Check on seat hydrogen and NO VERDICT exists; no judgment row and no enforcer row was written; cost 3.8227). The two marks of the entry are met as far as checked: debate_errors holds no "pkgX579" text for the run (its one row is the panel failure), and the run's row is saved. Re-calls ran through C1B and C2B (call_costs entries "C1B Call openrouter" and "C2B Call openrouter"; pkgBAR lines for DR1 and DR2), and C1B Extract is one of the six try nodes whose re-call no earlier run had shown. NOT CHECKED by W3: the report mark (the Drive file was not read). UNEXERCISED: the other five try nodes and D3B, C3B. This run is NOT a clean run: the panel failed and nothing after Panel Check ran (ASK 629), so it is not counted as one of the two live runs with no issues. The operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks two live runs with no issues; status stays 'read back'. RUN REVISION 42528 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed, that a path is unexercised, or what objective_met is, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42528-dqwbcshc (debate_results e0e528d8, row saved 22:59 CST 2026-11-24; launch 22:26 CST, ended with success 23:42 CST; engine 2df7f6fa and child aad0ad9c by the write records; google/gemini-4-hydrogen as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; every stage ran and no error row was written; outcome UNGRADED, panel 0-0 with 3 not counted under the debate rule; three judgments and 659 enforcer rows stored; cost 11.1907). Both marks of the entry are met: debate_errors holds no row for the run, so no "pkgX579" text, and the run's row is saved with an outcome. Second calls ran through C2B, C3G, D3B and D4B (call_costs; pkgBAR lines for DR2, CR3 and CR4), so C3G Extract, one of the six try nodes, and the D3B and C2B statements are now shown by a run. NOT CHECKED by W3: the report mark (the Drive file was not read). UNEXERCISED: C4G, D2B, C4B and C3B in this run. W3 counts this as the first of the two live runs with no issue that the operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks (AAR graded PASS by W1, Wall 11941); objective_met stays 'in part' and status stays 'read back' until the second.$t$,
